      "disposition": "Add :1030 to the D.110c-0b1/D.110c-c debt list and add one Batch-1 GREEN assertion that reopenCreatorSuccessorAdoption of an epoch>=2 successor still fails closed with the existing chain-invalid classification rather than activating."
    },
    {
      "title": "Batch-1 Node gate requires \"one browser lock\", which the Node realm cannot produce",
30→      "evidence": "plan :94176-94177 requires the focused Node test to prove \"one active topic owner and one browser lock\". packages/node/src/creator-adoption-activate.ts:106-114 browserLockRealm() requires window === globalThis or an object globalThis.location; the root suite runs in the default node environment (vite.config.mts:86-108 sets no test.environment), so acquireBrowserLock returns undefined and no lock exists. Satisfying the clause in Node would require synthesizing location/navigator.locks, i.e. a fake lock manager.",
